It calls the YouTube Data API v3 with the API key of the user, who accepts the
YouTube API Services Terms of Service, and reads the public RSS feeds and
thumbnails of YouTube. YouTube is a trademark of Google LLC; this integration
is not affiliated with, endorsed by nor sponsored by Google or YouTube.
The features follow the Home Assistant "YouTube" integration (Apache-2.0) and
its youtubeaio library (MIT): the Shorts check (HEAD /shorts/<id>) is the same
idea; no code is taken from them.
